1
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:05,510
Chocolates save us from many things, especially emotional distress.
巧克力能让我们免受许多事情的困扰，尤其是情绪上的痛苦。

2
00:00:06,310 --> 00:00:12,440
They comfort us in times of trouble, calming down a racing heart by channelling happy calories inside us.
身处困境时，它们给我们安慰：把带来快乐的热量输送到我们体内，从而让狂跳的心平静下来。

3
00:00:13,240 --> 00:00:16,370
We all have faith in chocolates to delight us in an instant!
我们都相信，巧克力能在转眼间让我们开心起来！

4
00:00:17,170 --> 00:00:24,030
Recently, chocolate lovers were heartbroken as scientists claimed that chocolates could become extinct by 2050!
最近，有科学家声称到2050年巧克力可能会灭绝，这让巧克力爱好者们心碎不已！

5
00:00:24,830 --> 00:00:27,340
But hey, we have some happy news for you.
不过，嘿，我们有一些好消息要告诉你。

6
00:00:28,140 --> 00:00:31,260
Scientists can still help save chocolates from dying out!
科学家仍然能够帮助巧克力免于灭绝！

7
00:00:32,060 --> 00:00:38,960
If you are not aware as to why scientists made the statement about the death of this wonderful thing, let us tell you the facts.
如果你不清楚科学家为何会就这一美妙之物的消亡发表这番言论，那就让我们把事实告诉你吧。

8
00:00:39,760 --> 00:00:48,730
Chocolate trees, whose seeds are used to make chocolate, grow in the tropical plant world and require very specific weather conditions to prosper.
可可树的种子用来制作巧克力；这种树生长在热带植物世界里，需要非常特定的天气条件才能茁壮成长。

9
00:00:49,530 --> 00:00:56,210
Now, fifty percent of the world’s cocoa beans come from two countries in West Africa: Côte d’Ivoire and Ghana.
目前，全世界百分之五十的可可豆来自西非的两个国家：科特迪瓦和加纳。

10
00:00:57,010 --> 00:01:09,110
Scientists believe that both of these countries will experience a 3.8 °F temperature increase by 2050 due to global warming, endangering the cacao farms in the rainforests.
科学家认为，由于全球变暖，到2050年这两个国家的气温都将上升3.8华氏度，危及雨林中的可可种植园。

11
00:01:09,910 --> 00:01:16,490
These farms will then have to be shifted to cooler mountainous areas, which are the natural habitat of wildlife.
届时，这些种植园将不得不迁往更凉爽的山区，而那里是野生动物的天然栖息地。

12
00:01:17,290 --> 00:01:22,210
This will lead to some tough decisions: whether to grow chocolate or save wildlife.
这将带来一些艰难的抉择：是种植巧克力，还是保护野生动物。

13
00:01:23,010 --> 00:01:32,690
Unfortunately, the crisis of global warming has already had a serious negative impact on cacao farms’ yields, leading to the prices of chocolates skyrocketing.
不幸的是，全球变暖危机已经对可可种植园的产量造成了严重的负面影响，导致巧克力价格飞涨。

14
00:01:33,490 --> 00:01:38,960
Scientists, however, are trying to find a long-term and eco-friendly solution to this problem!
然而，科学家们正设法为这一问题找到一个长期而又环保的解决方案！

15
00:01:39,760 --> 00:01:49,670
They are trying to modify the species with a gene-editing technology, which will transform the seedlings into a species that survives even in a drier and warmer climate.
他们正尝试用一种基因编辑技术改造这一物种，这项技术将把幼苗转变为一种即使在更干燥、更温暖的气候中也能存活的物种。

16
00:01:50,470 --> 00:02:04,950
According to a report by Business Insider, in the University of California’s new bio-sciences building, tiny green cacao seedlings are lined up in refrigerated greenhouses for a new experiment using a technology called CRISPR.
据《商业内幕》报道，在加利福尼亚大学新建的生物科学大楼里，小小的绿色可可树幼苗一排排地摆放在冷藏温室中，准备用于一项采用CRISPR技术的新实验。

17
00:02:05,750 --> 00:02:13,540
This technology, which manipulates the DNA of plants, is already being used across the world to make plants tougher and cheaper.
这项操控植物DNA的技术已在世界各地得到应用，用来让植物变得更强健、更便宜。

18
00:02:14,340 --> 00:02:25,800
Similarly, in this unconventional experiment, scientists will make tiny, precise changes to the DNA of the seedlings to make the cocoa crops survive in warmer and drier climates.
同样，在这项非常规的实验中，科学家们将对幼苗的DNA作出微小而精确的改动，让可可作物能在更温暖、更干燥的气候中存活。
